// A SOLUTION FILE, NOT A PROJECT. `files: []` is deliberate — the real configuration is in the two
// referenced projects — but it has a trap in it worth naming, because it cost this repo real
// confidence rather than merely being a curiosity.
//
// `npx tsc --noEmit` here type-checks EXACTLY NOTHING. It reads this file, finds an empty `files`
// array, ignores `references` entirely (only `-b`/`--build` follows those), and exits 0. It prints
// no warning and takes about a second, so it looks precisely like a passing type-check. It was
// reported as "tsc clean" three times in one session — including in commit messages — over a tree
// that had never been checked at all. `npx tsc --noEmit --listFiles | wc -l` answers 0, which is the
// quickest way to see it for yourself.
//
// The gate is `npm run typecheck` (`tsc -b --force`), which is what `npm run build` already ran and
// what CI must run. `--force` because `-b` is incremental and will happily skip work on the strength
// of a stale `.tsbuildinfo`, which is a second way to get a green result that means nothing.
{
  "files": [],
  // `tsconfig.scripts.json` EXISTED FOR A LONG TIME WITHOUT THIS LINE, which meant `tsc -b` never
  // built it and NOTHING under `scripts/` was type-checked by the gate — the entire keeper, the
  // verification scripts, the admin tools. That is precisely the failure this file's header
  // describes, one layer deeper: the header warns that `--noEmit` checks nothing because
  // `references` is ignored without `-b`, and the same blindness applied to a project that `-b`
  // would have followed if anyone had listed it. A missing reference is silent by construction —
  // there is no error for a project nobody asked about.
  //
  // Adding it surfaced exactly two errors across the whole directory, both the `Bun` global in
  // `verify-wallet-states.ts`, now declared locally. If a future project is added here and the gate
  // goes red on someone else's file, that is the reference working rather than a reason to remove it.
  "references": [
    { "path": "./tsconfig.app.json" },
    { "path": "./tsconfig.node.json" },
    { "path": "./tsconfig.e2e.json" },
    { "path": "./tsconfig.api.json" },
    { "path": "./tsconfig.scripts.json" }
  ]
}
